---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /editor/
noindex: true
# A noindex page has no business in the sitemap.
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
pageTitle: Profile editor
pageDescription: Local editing tool for this profile. Not profile content.
pageStyles: /assets/editor.css
pageScript: /assets/editor.js
---

{#
  Every section is a fieldset whose legend is a toggle button: the grouping
  stays semantic, the body collapses, and which sections are open is remembered
  in this browser. The chevron is inline rather than a background image so it
  can turn with the button's aria-expanded state.
#}
{% macro sectionHead(id, label, counts) %}
<legend>
  <button type="button" class="section-toggle" data-section-toggle="{{ id }}"
          aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="section-{{ id }}">
    <svg class="chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
         stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"/>
    </svg>
    <span>{{ label | safe }}</span>
    {#- The count is what a collapsed section still tells you, so it is filled in
        by the script on every render rather than only at build time. -#}
    {% if counts %}<span class="section-count" data-section-count="{{ id }}"></span>{% endif %}
  </button>
</legend>
{% endmacro %}

{#
  The row of controls above a repeatable list: how many entries it holds, and —
  for the lists with dates on them — a one-click way back to newest-first after
  dragging. Rendered here so the markup stays in the template, filled by the script.
#}
{% macro listTools(id, addLabel, dated) %}
<div class="list-tools">
  <p class="list-count muted" data-list-count="{{ id }}" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <span class="toolbar-spacer"></span>
  {#- Collapses the rows of this list only. The toolbar's Collapse all works on
      whole sections; this one is for the drop-downs inside one of them. It
      hides itself below two rows, where a row's own title is enough. -#}
  <button type="button" class="btn btn-small" data-rows-toggle="{{ id }}" hidden>Collapse all</button>
  {% if dated %}
  <button type="button" class="btn btn-small" data-sort="{{ id }}">Sort by date</button>
  {% endif %}
  <button type="button" class="btn btn-small" data-add="{{ id }}">{{ addLabel }}</button>
</div>
{% endmacro %}

<div class="editor" data-editor>
  <header class="editor-intro">
    <h1>Profile editor</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Fill this in, and it becomes the site. Everything you type is saved in this browser
      as you go, so a refresh or a closed tab loses nothing. Uploaded images are kept in
      this browser too.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Fields marked <span class="required">required</span> have no fallback in the
      published profile, so <strong>Download .json</strong> and <strong>Save to data/</strong>
      check them before they run. Everything else is optional.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Every section heading and every entry inside one opens and closes when you click it.
      <strong>Collapse all</strong> in the toolbar shuts every section; the one above each
      list shuts that list's entries. Which sections you left open is remembered in this
      browser, and a closed section is still saved and still published — collapsing only
      hides it here.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      <strong>The order you put things in is the order they are published.</strong> Drag a
      row by its handle (<span class="grip-inline" aria-hidden="true">⠿</span>) to move it,
      or focus the handle and press <kbd>↑</kbd>/<kbd>↓</kbd>. Nothing re-sorts behind your
      back, so put what you most want read at the top; <strong>Sort by date</strong> puts a
      list back in newest-first order whenever you want it.
    </p>
    <p class="muted" data-mode-note>Checking how this page is running…</p>
    {# Rows move without anything visible changing for a screen reader, so every
       move says where the row landed. #}
    <p class="visually-hidden" data-reorder-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  </header>

  <div class="editor-toolbar" role="group" aria-label="Save and export">
    <span class="save-status" data-save-status aria-live="polite">Loading…</span>
    <span class="toolbar-spacer"></span>
    <button type="button" class="btn" data-action="toggle-all" aria-live="polite">Collapse all</button>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-action="save-server" hidden>Save to data/</button>
    <button type="button" class="btn" data-action="export">Download .json</button>
    <button type="button" class="btn" data-action="import">Load .json</button>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-danger" data-action="reset">Clear all</button>
    <input type="file" accept="application/json,.json" data-import-input hidden>
  </div>

  <form class="editor-form" data-form autocomplete="on">

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("basics", "Basics") }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-basics">
        <div class="grid-2">
          <label>First name <span class="required">required</span>
            <input type="text" data-path="profile.firstName" autocomplete="given-name" required>
          </label>
          <label>Last name <span class="required">required</span>
            <input type="text" data-path="profile.lastName" autocomplete="family-name" required>
          </label>
        </div>
        <label>Headline <span class="required">required</span>
          <textarea rows="3" data-path="profile.headline"
            placeholder="Cloud Infrastructure Engineer" required></textarea>
          <small>Sits under your name. Line breaks are kept, so you can run it over more than one line.</small>
        </label>
        <div class="grid-2">
          <label>Location <span class="optional">optional</span>
            <input type="text" data-path="profile.location" placeholder="Amman, Jordan">
            <small>Leave blank to publish no location.</small>
          </label>
          <label>Pronouns <span class="optional">optional</span>
            <select data-path="profile.pronouns">
              <option value="">Not specified</option>
              <option value="he/him">he/him</option>
              <option value="she/her">she/her</option>
            </select>
            <small>Leave as Not specified to publish no pronouns at all.</small>
          </label>
        </div>
        <label>Email
          <input type="email" data-path="profile.email" autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@example.com">
          <small>Published in the HTML, the JSON-LD and /llms.txt. Leave blank to publish no email.</small>
        </label>

        <h3 class="subhead">Languages</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          Every language you can work in professionally, with your honest level. This is not
          decoration: the <strong>Language Gate</strong> that <code>/apply</code> and
          <code>/rank</code> run treats an undeclared language as a hard no rather than a gap
          to talk around, so leave out what you do not actually work in — and add what you do,
          or German-language postings cannot be scored at all.
        </p>
        <div data-list="languages" class="entry-editor-list"></div>
        {{ listTools("languages", "+ Add language", false) }}
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("about", "About") }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-about">
        <label>About me <span class="required">required</span>
          <textarea rows="7" data-path="profile.bio" required
            placeholder="Two to four sentences. Write it the way you would want an AI assistant to summarize you to someone else."></textarea>
          <small>The single most-quoted piece of text when an assistant summarizes you. State facts, not marketing.</small>
        </label>
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("education", "Education", true) }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-education">
        <div data-list="education" class="entry-editor-list"></div>
        {{ listTools("education", "+ Add education", true) }}
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("experience", "Experience", true) }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-experience">
        <div data-list="experience" class="entry-editor-list"></div>
        {{ listTools("experience", "+ Add position", true) }}
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("projects", "Projects", true) }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-projects">
        <p class="muted">
          Work you can point at that no employer owns: a side project, a university
          capstone, an open-source contribution. Published to <code>data/projects.json</code>,
          to <code>/llms.txt</code>, and as the <em>Independent Projects</em> section of the
          profile the job-search commands read.
        </p>
        <div data-list="projects" class="entry-editor-list"></div>
        {{ listTools("projects", "+ Add project", true) }}
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("certificates", "Licenses &amp; certifications", true) }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-certificates">
        <div data-list="certificates" class="entry-editor-list"></div>
        {{ listTools("certificates", "+ Add certification", true) }}
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("links", "Links", true) }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-links">
        <div data-list="links" class="entry-editor-list"></div>
        {{ listTools("links", "+ Add link", false) }}
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="collapsible">
      {{ sectionHead("skills", "Extra skills", true) }}
      <div class="section-body" id="section-skills">
        <p class="muted">
          Skills that no role, project or certificate already covers. The site unions these
          with every skill listed on a position, a project or a certification.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          Every skills box takes a whole list at once — paste one skill per line, or
          comma-separated. <strong>+ Add skills</strong> browses a catalogue by field and
          searches it, German labels included. <strong>From a job ad</strong> takes a pasted
          advert and pulls the skills out of it. The type-ahead offers your own skills first,
          then ones it has seen in adverts, then the catalogue — and anything you type is
          accepted whether or not it has heard of it. Duplicates are dropped whatever their
          capitalisation.
        </p>
        <div data-skills="profile.skills"></div>
      </div>
    </fieldset>
  </form>

  <section class="editor-help">
    <h2>What happens to this data</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing here is uploaded anywhere by the page itself. Text is stored in this browser's
      <code>localStorage</code> and images in its <code>IndexedDB</code>, both private to
      this browser on this device.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Download .json</strong> gives you one file containing everything, images
      included. To publish it, run <code>npm run import-data -- &lt;file&gt;</code> in the
      repository, then commit and push — the site rebuilds from it.
    </p>
    <p data-local-help hidden>
      Because you are running <code>npm run editor</code>, <strong>Save to data/</strong> is
      available and skips the download entirely: it writes
      <code>data/profile.json</code>, <code>data/experience.json</code>,
      <code>data/projects.json</code>, <code>data/certificates.json</code> and the images
      straight into the repository.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
